      "message": "Just so I understand the warning:\n`error: result of comparison of 30 \u003e\u003d 4-bit unsigned value is always true`\nmeans the SkNextLog2 is returning a 4-bit unsigned value (not an [8 bit] int as per the function call signature)? Is the compiler seeing the result (log_2(4096) \u003d 12) and saying \"oh, I can store this in a 4 bit unsigned\" and then \"oh hey, 15 (max for 4 bits) will always be less than 30?\n\nCould we cast the result instead of pushing the diagnostic?",
